    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `checkDigit` is a derived value on an owner, exactly analogous to the existing derived fields (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`), so I followed the same structure:\n\n1. **`model/LuhnCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility utility that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits of a string, mirroring the existing `LocalityResolver` helper style. This keeps the algorithm reusable and out of `Owner`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getCheckDigit()` that delegates to `LuhnCheckDigit.of(customerCode)` (null-safe when no customer code is set), placed alongside the other derived getters.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema. The generated `OwnerDto` picks it up and MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps `getCheckDigit()` \u2192 `checkDigit` automatically by name, so no mapper changes were needed.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit` \u2014 passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
